<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Keeps the live Claude OAuth session from reaching its hard 30-day expiry.

  The session expiry is claudeAiOauth.refreshTokenExpiresAt in the Keychain entry
  "Claude Code-credentials". Access-token refreshes never move it. When it lapsed on
  2026-10-29/30 the Mac sat logged out for ~2 days, because a logged-out machine cannot
  open a Claude tab to fix itself. This job reads that expiry once a day and, when fewer
  than 10 days remain (session older than ~20 days), forces a fresh login via
  scripts/account-switch.sh tate (with force-relogin and pin-target), then proves the
  expiry moved out past 25 days. Failure texts Tate over the free iMessage path.

  WHY LAUNCHD. It must run when Claude cannot, so it is node + security + canonical CDP
  only, with no Claude budget and no Supabase in the path.

  WHY THE CELLAR NODE. Full Disk Access (chat.db) and Automation (Messages) are keyed to
  the exact node binary, and the 2026-10-23 relink left /opt/homebrew/bin/node without
  either, so a failure text from this job would hang and never send. 22.22.3 still holds
  both; it loads with the compat dylib on DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH. Doctrine:
  a-node-relink-revokes-full-disk-access-for-launchd-jobs-2026-10-26.md

  CADENCE. Daily at 17:43 AEST plus RunAtLoad. A calendar fire missed while the Mac sleeps
  runs once on wake; RunAtLoad covers a reboot. A plain 14-day StartInterval would reset on
  every reboot and never catch up, and a single missed fire there could lose the whole
  margin. Here a missed fire costs one day of a 10-day window, and every day inside the
  window is another attempt.

  Install:
    cp launchd/au.ecodia.claude-relogin-guard.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/au.ecodia.claude-relogin-guard.plist
  Verify:   launchctl list | grep claude-relogin-guard
  Manual:   node scripts/claude-relogin-guard.js check   (prefix with two dashes; also: force, selftest)
  Doctrine: ecodiaos backend patterns/claude-oauth-session-is-30-days-and-only-a-relogin-resets-it-2026-10-30.md
-->
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>au.ecodia.claude-relogin-guard</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key><array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/Cellar/node@22/22.22.3/bin/node</string>
    <string>/Users/ecodia/.code/eos-laptop-agent/scripts/claude-relogin-guard.js</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/ecodia/.code/eos-laptop-agent</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key><dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>HOME</key><string>/Users/ecodia</string>
    <key>DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH</key><string>/Users/ecodia/.ecodiaos/node22-compat/lib</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key><dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>17</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>43</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/ecodia/Library/Logs/ecodiaos/claude-relogin-guard.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/ecodia/Library/Logs/ecodiaos/claude-relogin-guard.log</string>
</dict></plist>
